 "final_text": "The proof is done. `/work/putnam_2013_b4.lean` compiles with no errors and no warnings, and no `sorry` remains.\n\nThe argument: the mean minimizes the squared deviation, so Var(fg) \u2264 \u222b(fg \u2212 \u03bcf\u00b7\u03bcg)\u00b2. Writing fg \u2212 \u03bcf\u00b7\u03bcg = (f\u2212\u03bcf)\u00b7g + \u03bcf\u00b7(g\u2212\u03bcg) and using (u+v)\u00b2 \u2264 2u\u00b2 + 2v\u00b2 pointwise gives \u2264 2\u222b(f\u2212\u03bcf)\u00b2g\u00b2 + 2\u03bcf\u00b2\u00b7Var g. Then g\u00b2 \u2264 M(g)\u00b2 bounds the first term by 2M(g)\u00b2\u00b7Var f, and |\u03bcf| \u2264 M(f) bounds the second by 2M(f)\u00b2\u00b7Var g.\n\nThe imports, theorem statement, and hypotheses are unchanged. I used no axioms, `sorry`, `admit`, `native_decide`, `#eval`, or metaprogramming. I deleted my scratch files, so `/work` contains only the proof file.",
